1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,131 --> 00:00:17,600
I've got a little surprise for you. To make things more exciting.

9
00:00:17,632 --> 00:00:18,633
Just give me a moment.

10
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,634
Ta.

11
00:00:21,651 --> 00:00:23,680
If you want to have fun, you'll have to be patient, Director.

12
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,400
- Ta!
- She left ages ago.

13
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:29,640
She tricked you into booking this hotel room.

14
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:31,720
Then she lured me here, hoping we'd end up fighting.

15
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:32,783
I don't believe you!

16
00:00:32,818 --> 00:00:33,819
What are you doing?

17
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:37,211
I've already proven to you that there's nothing wrong with me in bed.

18
00:00:37,226 --> 00:00:39,200
We could even see a marriage counselor together.

19
00:00:39,382 --> 00:00:40,440
See? This is exactly why.

20
00:00:40,566 --> 00:00:42,240
I went to get some toys from my car.

21
00:00:42,283 --> 00:00:44,059
But I ran into Nopnapha.

22
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:46,840
Now I'm starting to wonder why you still won't divorce her.

23
00:00:46,854 --> 00:00:48,000
Could it be that you still love her?

24
00:00:48,055 --> 00:00:50,360
But you're the only one in my heart.

25
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:54,600
This year's New Year's party, they said each department

26
00:00:54,816 --> 00:00:56,427
should put on one performance.

27
00:00:56,571 --> 00:00:58,960
But that means our division has to put on a show, too.

28
00:00:59,024 --> 00:01:00,240
What are you performing at the New Year's party?

29
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,400
I'm not performing with them.

30
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,800
Then why don't you perform with me?

31
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,151
- I'll show my magic tricks.
- Sure.

32
00:01:05,502 --> 00:01:06,590
I'll perform with you.

33
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,280
Jolene, watch my livestream during the performance.

34
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,680
And when the big moment comes,

35
00:01:10,819 --> 00:01:13,760
Take screenshots. Post them on every social media platform as fast as you can.

36
00:01:14,024 --> 00:01:15,955
This is going to be so much fun, Nopnapha will scream.

37
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,601
[Thai Pattana Party]

38
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,250
A hot drink for you.

39
00:01:54,232 --> 00:01:55,233
Thank you.

40
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,560
I was just getting sleepy.

41
00:02:00,427 --> 00:02:01,560
Oh, it's tea.

42
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,920
Could I have coffee instead? Sorry.

43
00:02:05,558 --> 00:02:07,250
But it's already half past midnight.

44
00:02:07,723 --> 00:02:10,320
I brought you chamomile tea on purpose, ma'am.

45
00:02:10,646 --> 00:02:11,920
It'll help you sleep better.

46
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:17,051
I'm the first to speak in tomorrow's debate.

47
00:02:18,059 --> 00:02:21,640
The whole country will be watching. I won't be able to sleep.

48
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,800
Thank you for the tea, though.

49
00:02:25,712 --> 00:02:27,440
I'd rather have coffee.

50
00:02:27,707 --> 00:02:30,640
Of course. I'll get you a coffee.

51
00:02:42,694 --> 00:02:44,280
If you need anything else,

52
00:02:44,912 --> 00:02:46,160
just let me know.

53
00:02:46,523 --> 00:02:48,000
I'll be on standby in the next room.

54
00:02:49,632 --> 00:02:50,904
And in the lounge,

55
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,960
there's a large sofa bed.

56
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:58,400
In case you'd like to take a nap.

57
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,001
Don't worry.

58
00:03:02,464 --> 00:03:03,880
There's no one else in the building

59
00:03:05,371 --> 00:03:06,400
except the two of us.

60
00:03:16,323 --> 00:03:17,324
I'm pregnant.

61
00:03:20,595 --> 00:03:21,596
What?

62
00:03:22,292 --> 00:03:23,293
I'm sorry.

63
00:03:24,894 --> 00:03:26,000
I should've been more careful.

64
00:03:27,619 --> 00:03:30,424
Here's what we'll do. I'll take you to my friend's clinic.

65
00:03:30,808 --> 00:03:31,889
He can take care of it.

66
00:03:32,606 --> 00:03:33,607
No.

67
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:36,560
I'm not having an abortion.

68
00:03:38,011 --> 00:03:39,424
I'm keeping this baby no matter what.

69
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,627
But the election is just around the corner.

70
00:03:42,171 --> 00:03:43,974
How can you campaign with a big belly?

71
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:45,880
Why couldn't I?

72
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,201
A pregnant woman on the campaign trail

73
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,491
might win even more votes from women.

74
00:03:55,934 --> 00:03:56,935
Phop.

75
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:58,901
Let's get married.

76
00:04:10,544 --> 00:04:13,640
I know I'm not as capable as you.

77
00:04:15,584 --> 00:04:17,800
And I'll never rise as high as you.

78
00:04:22,352 --> 00:04:23,520
But I promise you

79
00:04:25,753 --> 00:04:26,880
I'll love you

80
00:04:28,414 --> 00:04:30,200
and always stand by your side.

81
00:04:36,731 --> 00:04:39,094
I'll have a one-of-a-kind ring made

82
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:41,560
just for you.

83
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,560
Because you're the most special person in my life.

84
00:06:08,144 --> 00:06:09,960
Let's meet at our usual hotel tonight.

85
00:06:10,432 --> 00:06:13,840
Let me make up for last time.

86
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:16,793
Oh, by the way, Ta.

87
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,840
That toy you said you'd use on me...

88
00:06:21,571 --> 00:06:22,600
Don't forget to bring it.

89
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,480
I'm busy these days.

90
00:06:24,734 --> 00:06:27,160
I won't be free until after New Year's.

91
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,640
What? Why?

92
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,880
What are you doing that's keeping you so busy?

93
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,200
I have to rehearse for the New Year's show with Veekit.

94
00:06:34,566 --> 00:06:35,567
What?

95
00:06:37,776 --> 00:06:39,360
How did you end up performing with him?

96
00:06:40,064 --> 00:06:41,065
He invited me.

97
00:06:41,312 --> 00:06:43,360
I thought it sounded interesting, so I said yes.

98
00:06:44,176 --> 00:06:45,760
You didn't invite me yourself, Director.

99
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,801
Just wait till you see my show with Veekit.

100
00:06:49,336 --> 00:06:50,337
Ta.

101
00:06:51,427 --> 00:06:52,428
Ta.

102
00:07:14,728 --> 00:07:16,129
Don't you have to pick up the kids from school?

103
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,840
I asked Oshi to pick them up instead.

104
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:24,721
Hey.

105
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,480
Can you make a rabbit appear? I want one.

106
00:07:39,939 --> 00:07:41,140
You should've told me earlier.

107
00:07:42,315 --> 00:07:44,656
I'll bring one tomorrow. Here, take this for now.

108
00:07:45,435 --> 00:07:46,436
I'm just kidding.

109
00:07:47,584 --> 00:07:50,230
So, what exactly do we have to do?

110
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:54,400
Nothing much. Just hand me the props.

111
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,840
Oh, but let's practice this trick first.

112
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,101
Here.

113
00:08:02,598 --> 00:08:04,180
You'll have to get inside this box.

114
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:06,450
There's a hidden compartment inside.

115
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,901
Here, come over here.

116
00:08:09,696 --> 00:08:11,600
And when I open the box again,

117
00:08:12,526 --> 00:08:13,840
it'll be empty.

118
00:08:14,766 --> 00:08:17,360
But it'll be a bit dark and cramped in there.

119
00:08:22,982 --> 00:08:23,983
You'll be okay, right?

120
00:08:28,848 --> 00:08:29,849
Yeah.

121
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:32,150
No problem at all.

122
00:08:38,579 --> 00:08:40,200
Why do you want to do a magic show?

123
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,201
Ta.

124
00:09:05,691 --> 00:09:06,720
Look, I've got this trick too.

125
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:14,720
Wow! How did you do that?

126
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,000
Have you been practicing for days?

127
00:09:19,616 --> 00:09:20,720
I've been doing magic since I was a kid.

128
00:09:21,211 --> 00:09:23,160
I was a big fan of Criss Angel. He was so cool.

129
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:24,560
I wanted to be cool like him.

130
00:09:26,102 --> 00:09:28,360
Who's Criss Angel?

131
00:09:28,848 --> 00:09:30,200
An American magician.

132
00:09:30,836 --> 00:09:32,320
The one with the rock-star look.

133
00:09:39,408 --> 00:09:42,176
What's wrong? I just asked why you wanted to do a magic show.

134
00:09:44,472 --> 00:09:45,848
I was a big fan of Criss Angel.

135
00:09:46,536 --> 00:09:48,160
I thought he was so cool when I was a kid.

136
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,120
I wanted to be like him, so I started practicing.

137
00:09:50,712 --> 00:09:52,320
Who's Criss Angel?

138
00:09:59,552 --> 00:10:02,240
An American magician with a rock-star look.

139
00:10:05,416 --> 00:10:07,180
Come on, what else can you show me?

140
00:10:21,910 --> 00:10:24,440
Wow, I can't believe you can do that too!

141
00:10:25,296 --> 00:10:26,297
What else have you got?

142
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:27,791
What does this one do?

143
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,471
Pretty good, huh?

144
00:11:00,518 --> 00:11:01,519
Where's Ta?

145
00:11:02,763 --> 00:11:04,720
We finished rehearsing. She just left.

146
00:11:21,075 --> 00:11:22,760
Stop being so stubborn, Veekit.

147
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:25,440
You're only going to annoy her.

148
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:27,600
But even after she found out I was pursuing her,

149
00:11:28,832 --> 00:11:30,920
she still agreed to do the magic show with me.

150
00:11:31,936 --> 00:11:34,267
- What does that tell you?
- She's just doing it to spite me.

151
00:11:35,102 --> 00:11:36,103
Because...

152
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,600
I slept with Napha the other day.

153
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:43,701
She'll never be interested in you, Veekit.

154
00:11:44,131 --> 00:11:45,280
Stop dreaming.

155
00:11:46,936 --> 00:11:48,947
But your relationship with Ta...

156
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,440
- is impossible too.
- Why would it be?

157
00:11:52,206 --> 00:11:53,416
We're in love.

158
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:58,000
And I'm not treating her like a toy, as you think.

159
00:12:00,462 --> 00:12:03,600
I've never loved any woman this much before.

160
00:12:04,536 --> 00:12:05,537
I mean it.

161
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:10,200
So stop trying to steal Ta from me.

162
00:12:10,755 --> 00:12:11,756
I won't let you have her.

163
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,921
[Fun Finance Party! Happy New Year 2026]

164
00:12:49,246 --> 00:12:50,920
Hello, hello. One, two, three.

165
00:12:51,987 --> 00:12:53,388
Our next performance

166
00:12:53,931 --> 00:12:56,180
is one I'm especially excited to present

167
00:12:57,014 --> 00:12:58,520
from the Corporate Relations Department.

168
00:12:59,184 --> 00:13:03,480
Please give them your support.

169
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:28,320
♪ Just one glance at you ♪

170
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:31,480
♪ And I knew you'd stolen my heart ♪

171
00:13:31,835 --> 00:13:34,320
♪ I wish I could tell you how cute you are ♪

172
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,101
♪ But I don't want to come on too strong ♪

173
00:13:42,192 --> 00:13:44,500
Is that all you've got? You call that dancing?

174
00:13:44,923 --> 00:13:47,040
Watch me. Come on!

175
00:13:48,192 --> 00:13:51,193
♪ I wish I could say, Call me when you get home ♪

176
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:56,320
♪ Anyone else who calls will hear my ringback tone... ♪

177
00:13:57,072 --> 00:14:01,600
Wow! If they sing "Do Re Mi" or "Kin Jub Jib",

178
00:14:01,622 --> 00:14:02,760
I'll go up there and give them a tip.

179
00:14:05,024 --> 00:14:06,025
Don't you agree, darling?

180
00:14:06,443 --> 00:14:11,600
♪ Welcome to the heart deposit service ♪

181
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:16,520
♪ Register your heart and take your number ♪

182
00:14:16,561 --> 00:14:18,520
♪ Leave your heart in safe hands ♪

183
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,001
Where are you going?

184
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,501
To take a piss.

185
00:14:25,901 --> 00:14:30,040
♪ Leave your heart with me ♪

186
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:33,701
♪ Let's exchange numbers, oh, oh, oh! ♪

187
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:44,751
Director.

188
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:47,080
Want something even more exciting?

189
00:14:48,392 --> 00:14:49,520
Even more exciting?

190
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:52,360
I'm already getting so turned on, Ta.

191
00:14:52,470 --> 00:14:55,600
Oh, you've got a little tail too. I love it.

192
00:14:58,323 --> 00:14:59,324
Director.

193
00:15:01,592 --> 00:15:03,080
I've got a special surprise for you.

194
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,520
I love this side of you, Ta.

195
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,920
You should've told me you liked tight spaces.

196
00:15:20,134 --> 00:15:21,135
Let me take that off for you.

197
00:15:22,326 --> 00:15:23,560
You take yours off first, Director.

198
00:15:24,255 --> 00:15:26,080
Come here. Let me help you.

199
00:15:42,731 --> 00:15:46,220
Director, let me grab a toy to spice things up.

200
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:47,911
A toy?

201
00:15:48,515 --> 00:15:49,516
To spice things up?

202
00:15:50,339 --> 00:15:52,680
Why bother leaving the last piece on?

203
00:15:55,011 --> 00:15:57,240
Ta... Sweetheart?

204
00:15:58,742 --> 00:15:59,743
Ta? Ta!

205
00:16:03,163 --> 00:16:04,480
Whoa! What the hell?

206
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:06,440
Why is it so cramped in here?

207
00:16:22,206 --> 00:16:23,207
Ta!

208
00:16:23,318 --> 00:16:24,720
It's our turn. Let's go.

209
00:16:35,467 --> 00:16:37,600
Ta, sweetheart! Where are you?

210
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,240
I can't get out, Ta!

211
00:16:41,230 --> 00:16:45,000
Thank you all for sitting through the entire show.

212
00:16:45,691 --> 00:16:49,200
If you're in the bathroom, hurry back.

213
00:16:49,552 --> 00:16:51,200
Especially you ladies!

214
00:16:51,542 --> 00:16:53,280
Because our next act

215
00:16:53,568 --> 00:16:59,232
is a magic show by Veekit from the Personnel Department.

216
00:17:03,568 --> 00:17:05,169
Veekit is so handsome.

217
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:06,640
Veekit!

218
00:17:43,979 --> 00:17:45,320
Oh! A bird!

219
00:17:45,878 --> 00:17:46,960
That's right!

220
00:17:47,168 --> 00:17:51,369
And more importantly, it looks classier than a swan.

221
00:18:09,398 --> 00:18:10,880
Where did the bottle go?

222
00:18:11,174 --> 00:18:13,850
Exactly! Won't the glass shatter in his hand?

223
00:18:15,424 --> 00:18:16,840
What's that on the table?

224
00:18:17,046 --> 00:18:18,047
That's a candle.

225
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,080
It looks so tempting to sit on.

226
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:22,881
Hey! Hey!

227
00:18:24,043 --> 00:18:26,760
Hey, what if we actually work at the Ministry of Magic?

228
00:18:26,971 --> 00:18:28,800
You're right! Dumbledore! Dumbledore!

229
00:18:29,867 --> 00:18:30,868
Hagrid!

230
00:18:32,811 --> 00:18:33,812
Dobby!

231
00:18:43,147 --> 00:18:44,148
What's that?

232
00:18:44,411 --> 00:18:45,830
Ooh, what's happening? This is exciting.

233
00:18:51,412 --> 00:18:52,413
Ta.

234
00:18:52,968 --> 00:18:53,969
Oh, come on.

235
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:55,521
Ta!

236
00:19:27,971 --> 00:19:29,560
Serves that homewrecker right. She's gone.

237
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:30,841
Exactly, Auntie!

238
00:20:14,896 --> 00:20:16,360
Now I see why

239
00:20:16,544 --> 00:20:18,840
you have so many girls, sir.

240
00:20:19,062 --> 00:20:20,841
Anaconda!

241
00:20:20,955 --> 00:20:22,600
Boa... Nguu yak!

242
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:26,080
Eww! A snake! I'm scared of snakes.

243
00:20:28,379 --> 00:20:30,920
That black magic is powerful.

244
00:20:31,488 --> 00:20:33,250
Do you believe in the Naga?

245
00:20:35,379 --> 00:20:37,960
- Zoom in! Zoom in!
- Send it to me too!

246
00:20:42,219 --> 00:20:44,520
Looks like we're getting a bonus!

247
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,480
What a wonderful show, everyone.

248
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,760
You've really done our ministry proud.

249
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,200
Give them a round of applause.

250
00:21:18,532 --> 00:21:21,080
That was one hell of a show.

251
00:21:21,416 --> 00:21:22,560
What a huge show!

252
00:21:23,363 --> 00:21:25,720
That was spectacular! Wow!

253
00:21:29,838 --> 00:21:32,440
A bright new year dawns upon our nation.

254
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:35,240
May joy and prosperity spread throughout the land.

255
00:21:35,571 --> 00:21:38,400
Together, we shall build a thriving nation.

256
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:41,220
United as one, the people and government stand.

257
00:21:41,352 --> 00:21:43,200
I, Narong Kuldamrongkitti,

258
00:21:43,438 --> 00:21:45,680
the Prime Minister, together with my Cabinet,

259
00:21:45,816 --> 00:21:49,400
would like to wish all Thai citizens

260
00:21:49,803 --> 00:21:50,804
a very Happy New Year.

261
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,801
- Happy New Year!
- Happy New Year!

262
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:55,721
Cut!

263
00:22:03,998 --> 00:22:04,999
Ms. Nopnapha.

264
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:07,480
Do you have any other appointments?

265
00:22:08,512 --> 00:22:11,003
I have a meeting with the central bank governor, sir.

266
00:22:11,286 --> 00:22:12,560
Is there something you need, Prime Minister?

267
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,041
Postpone it.

268
00:22:14,966 --> 00:22:16,078
There's something I want to discuss with you.

269
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,001
Of course.

270
00:22:32,656 --> 00:22:34,320
My face when I see this semester's grades.

271
00:22:35,147 --> 00:22:37,600
My face watching the Asian Games opening ceremony.

272
00:22:38,278 --> 00:22:41,360
My face when I wake up and Narong is still Prime Minister.

273
00:22:50,758 --> 00:22:52,120
How do you feel when you see these videos?

274
00:22:55,371 --> 00:22:58,000
I think kids these days are very creative.

275
00:22:58,022 --> 00:23:00,440
And they have a good sense of humor too.

276
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:04,640
You're turning the government into a laughingstock.

277
00:23:05,872 --> 00:23:07,720
And undermining its credibility.

278
00:23:11,664 --> 00:23:13,360
The government's credibility

279
00:23:14,550 --> 00:23:16,480
depends on whether we can deliver

280
00:23:16,551 --> 00:23:18,520
on our campaign promises.

281
00:23:19,248 --> 00:23:20,800
And according to the polls,

282
00:23:21,158 --> 00:23:24,440
the three ministries under my party's control

283
00:23:24,774 --> 00:23:27,400
have the highest public approval ratings.

284
00:23:29,344 --> 00:23:30,560
As for personal gain,

285
00:23:31,086 --> 00:23:34,087
I've never been careless enough to get caught,

286
00:23:34,296 --> 00:23:36,180
unlike certain other ministers.

287
00:23:38,296 --> 00:23:41,050
My husband just put on a raunchy show at a party.

288
00:23:41,989 --> 00:23:44,595
I doubt that threatens the government's stability.

289
00:23:45,379 --> 00:23:47,235
Good performance is certainly important.

290
00:23:48,948 --> 00:23:52,800
But I'm talking about a minister who delivers results

291
00:23:53,102 --> 00:23:54,360
and maintains a good public image,

292
00:23:55,416 --> 00:23:57,678
versus one who delivers results but has a tarnished reputation.

293
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,640
Which one do you think I'd choose?

294
00:24:03,736 --> 00:24:06,737
I can't control my husband's performances.

295
00:24:07,592 --> 00:24:09,560
That's not a minister's responsibility.

296
00:24:10,557 --> 00:24:14,280
My duty is to deliver great results for the people.

297
00:24:17,395 --> 00:24:18,478
That's just how women are.

298
00:24:19,502 --> 00:24:20,503
What do you mean by that?

299
00:24:21,150 --> 00:24:22,920
You can't even control your own husband.

300
00:24:24,374 --> 00:24:25,575
So if one day

301
00:24:25,979 --> 00:24:28,294
he commits a serious crime,

302
00:24:28,368 --> 00:24:30,520
like rape, murder, or drug trafficking,

303
00:24:30,980 --> 00:24:32,680
will you still say it has nothing to do with you

304
00:24:33,232 --> 00:24:35,680
and won't affect the government?

305
00:24:42,283 --> 00:24:46,800
Prime Minister, I think at the next Cabinet reshuffle meeting,

306
00:24:47,195 --> 00:24:49,850
this issue should be at the top of the agenda.

307
00:24:52,758 --> 00:24:53,810
Prime Minister, please.

308
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,998
If you remove me from my position,

309
00:24:57,280 --> 00:24:59,250
you'll be playing right into the opposition's hands.

310
00:25:00,123 --> 00:25:02,280
They're the ones who leaked the video

311
00:25:02,558 --> 00:25:04,600
and spread those memes to discredit me.

312
00:25:07,262 --> 00:25:08,680
From what I've heard,

313
00:25:09,365 --> 00:25:12,250
the first person to share the video wasn't from the opposition.

314
00:25:14,382 --> 00:25:15,800
It was a woman named

315
00:25:17,070 --> 00:25:18,071
Mutta.

316
00:25:24,664 --> 00:25:25,840
I've known about this for a long time,

317
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,360
but I didn't want to bring it up

318
00:25:28,910 --> 00:25:30,500
because I considered it a personal matter.

319
00:25:33,085 --> 00:25:36,320
But things have gone too far now. Deal with it quickly.

320
00:25:37,443 --> 00:25:40,320
I care more about the government's image than its achievements.

321
00:25:48,379 --> 00:25:50,459
It's 4 p.m. Office hours are over.

322
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,500
Come back tomorrow at nine.

323
00:25:53,987 --> 00:25:55,320
But if it were that bitch Mutta,

324
00:25:56,259 --> 00:25:58,920
you'd be open for business 24 hours a day, wouldn't you?

325
00:26:02,707 --> 00:26:03,708
Of course.

326
00:26:05,411 --> 00:26:07,100
You got so close to her

327
00:26:07,412 --> 00:26:09,760
without realizing she was plotting to destroy us.

328
00:26:11,123 --> 00:26:12,662
Having a cheating husband

329
00:26:12,752 --> 00:26:14,760
- isn't as embarrassing as having a stupid one.
- Watch it!

330
00:26:16,753 --> 00:26:18,667
If your blood sugar's low, go drink something sweet.

331
00:26:19,154 --> 00:26:20,680
Don't take it out on your husband.

332
00:26:21,846 --> 00:26:24,320
You're lucky you're only getting yelled at by your wife.

333
00:26:24,467 --> 00:26:26,168
I got chewed out by the Prime Minister.

334
00:26:27,491 --> 00:26:29,650
The entire Cabinet knows about that bitch Mutta now.

335
00:26:31,272 --> 00:26:33,920
If I can't even deal with one lousy mistress,

336
00:26:34,286 --> 00:26:35,760
they're going to kick me out of office.

337
00:26:39,550 --> 00:26:41,560
You're scared of a stupid threat like that?

338
00:26:43,368 --> 00:26:46,760
Come on, you've got 120 MPs. What's there to fear?

339
00:26:47,283 --> 00:26:50,880
If they keep threatening you, just join the opposition.

340
00:26:51,502 --> 00:26:53,760
A minority government won't survive anyway.

341
00:26:54,032 --> 00:26:56,960
Come on! You're a rising political star right now.

342
00:26:57,126 --> 00:27:00,080
You'll win by a landslide in the next election.

343
00:27:01,344 --> 00:27:03,840
Good thing I never let you go into politics.

344
00:27:04,784 --> 00:27:07,640
Do you really think that if I join the opposition,

345
00:27:07,685 --> 00:27:09,360
all those MPs will follow me?

346
00:27:09,867 --> 00:27:12,960
And more importantly, if I haven't launched the Smart Card project,

347
00:27:13,115 --> 00:27:15,160
what will I campaign on in the next election?

348
00:27:19,083 --> 00:27:20,084
Phop.

349
00:27:20,822 --> 00:27:22,390
If you won't do it for me,

350
00:27:23,195 --> 00:27:24,800
then do it for yourself.

351
00:27:26,342 --> 00:27:29,480
Because the higher I rise, the higher you'll rise with me.

352
00:27:30,102 --> 00:27:31,203
But if I fall,

353
00:27:31,798 --> 00:27:34,500
you'll be nothing more than a lowly civil servant.

354
00:27:36,899 --> 00:27:40,120
Stay away from that bitch Mutta, for your own sake.

355
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:52,768
Touch and Oshi,

356
00:27:53,904 --> 00:27:56,700
we need to find a way to get rid of that bitch once and for all.

357
00:28:37,928 --> 00:28:38,829
What?

358
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:41,040
Someone's following me in a car.

359
00:28:42,211 --> 00:28:45,120
I think she's making her move. She's sent someone to kill me.

360
00:28:45,472 --> 00:28:48,200
Seriously? Your dashcam's recording, right?

361
00:28:48,758 --> 00:28:50,960
Yeah, both front and rear cameras.

362
00:28:51,707 --> 00:28:52,920
Get over here right now.

363
00:28:53,264 --> 00:28:54,840
And bring the phone signal detector.

364
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:56,640
Okay. Be careful.

365
00:29:35,227 --> 00:29:36,400
What is it, Mr. Thaithat?

366
00:29:36,736 --> 00:29:38,360
She sent me to escort you to see her.

367
00:29:38,811 --> 00:29:40,160
She's waiting at the Ministry.

368
00:29:42,556 --> 00:29:43,557
Okay.

369
00:29:54,608 --> 00:29:55,609
Hey.

370
00:29:56,384 --> 00:29:57,885
She wants me to meet her at the Ministry.

371
00:29:58,123 --> 00:29:59,320
That's dangerous.

372
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,560
If she locks you in a room and kills you, no one will ever know.

373
00:30:02,616 --> 00:30:04,120
Then I'll turn on my voice recorder.

374
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:05,841
If she tries anything,

375
00:30:06,441 --> 00:30:07,480
you'll have evidence.

376
00:30:07,584 --> 00:30:09,240
Hey, isn't that too risky?

377
00:30:28,336 --> 00:30:29,520
May I see your phone, please?

378
00:30:52,056 --> 00:30:53,057
This way, please.

379
00:31:10,096 --> 00:31:13,360
Isn't summoning someone after office hours against regulations?

380
00:31:13,414 --> 00:31:14,415
[Nopnapha Jetsadaphiban]

381
00:31:14,420 --> 00:31:15,480
[Minister of Digital Finance]

382
00:31:24,056 --> 00:31:25,357
Are you going to stand there and talk?

383
00:31:31,491 --> 00:31:32,960
No need to be so nervous.

384
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:36,160
This isn't a Committee Hearing Room.

385
00:31:37,598 --> 00:31:40,300
Just a wife wanting to talk to her husband's mistress.

386
00:31:42,170 --> 00:31:43,171
I'm honored.

387
00:31:43,326 --> 00:31:45,982
To be summoned here by you for a personal matter.

388
00:31:47,206 --> 00:31:48,207
Yes.

389
00:31:48,518 --> 00:31:50,480
It should've been a private matter.

390
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:53,760
But you made it public

391
00:31:54,464 --> 00:31:56,920
the day you forced Phop to put on that show onstage.

392
00:31:59,065 --> 00:32:01,766
No, it was started when you slapped me down the Ministry steps.

393
00:32:02,384 --> 00:32:04,240
People have been gossiping about us for ages.

394
00:32:04,870 --> 00:32:06,071
What are you so afraid of?

395
00:32:07,264 --> 00:32:08,800
And let me make one thing clear.

396
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:11,001
From now on,

397
00:32:12,086 --> 00:32:16,160
I'll be even more affectionate with the Director in public.

398
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:20,160
Especially when you're watching.

399
00:32:21,339 --> 00:32:22,340
Do you know why?

400
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:26,600
Because you're a rotten little bitch.

401
00:32:27,686 --> 00:32:29,520
Because I know there's nothing you can do

402
00:32:30,251 --> 00:32:31,252
but sit there and take it.

403
00:32:32,816 --> 00:32:34,040
And next time,

404
00:32:34,742 --> 00:32:36,443
I'll smile at you again.

405
00:32:37,163 --> 00:32:39,000
I just love the look on your face.

406
00:32:39,520 --> 00:32:42,600
It's hilarious. I could make so many more memes out of it.

407
00:33:18,011 --> 00:33:19,012
Ten million.

408
00:33:23,230 --> 00:33:25,760
I hope that's enough to buy my husband back.

409
00:33:32,710 --> 00:33:36,080
The Director's worth more than ten million in bed.

410
00:33:39,280 --> 00:33:41,552
This isn't a government procurement deal

411
00:33:41,659 --> 00:33:43,250
that you can close by throwing money at it.

412
00:33:46,896 --> 00:33:47,897
Keep your money.

413
00:33:48,726 --> 00:33:50,700
You might need it to pay for a man someday.

414
00:33:53,144 --> 00:33:54,145
Thank you

415
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,040
for letting me live this long,

416
00:33:57,801 --> 00:34:00,250
so I can keep enjoying myself with the Director.

417
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:04,440
And watch you suffer like this for a long time to come.

418
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:06,601
If you'll excuse me.

419
00:34:09,451 --> 00:34:10,452
You bitch, Mutta!

420
00:34:10,837 --> 00:34:12,320
Come here! Come here!

421
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:14,121
Get over here!

422
00:34:15,376 --> 00:34:19,440
I'll kill you, Mutta! You homewrecking bitch!

423
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:27,050
Ma'am, what's going on?

424
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:28,880
I'll kill her!

425
00:34:29,454 --> 00:34:30,797
- I'll kill her!
- Calm down, ma'am. Please calm down.

426
00:34:32,195 --> 00:34:34,400
Call a hitman and have her shot right now!

427
00:34:34,488 --> 00:34:36,560
We can't do that, ma'am. It's too risky.

428
00:34:36,691 --> 00:34:40,400
And did throwing money at her like you suggested work? Huh?

429
00:34:40,493 --> 00:34:42,382
- I'll kill her!
- Please calm down, ma'am.

430
00:34:45,069 --> 00:34:49,040
Ma'am, now that photos of the Director with a sex doll have leaked,

431
00:34:49,070 --> 00:34:51,600
are you worried about the damage to your reputation?

432
00:34:52,635 --> 00:34:54,960
Not at all. It was just an internal celebration.

433
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:57,200
It may have been a little risqué, that's all.

434
00:34:57,539 --> 00:34:59,140
But the younger staff seemed to enjoy it.

435
00:34:59,160 --> 00:35:00,760
They didn't expect the Director to go all out like that.

436
00:35:02,971 --> 00:35:06,600
I think we should talk about the Smart Card project instead.

437
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:07,801
Oh, yes.

438
00:35:07,810 --> 00:35:10,523
How far along is the Smart Card project now?

439
00:35:10,896 --> 00:35:14,600
We've already issued an invitation to bid through e-bidding.

440
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:17,490
We haven't made the terms of reference too restrictive,

441
00:35:17,500 --> 00:35:20,680
because we want to give young entrepreneurs and smaller companies

442
00:35:20,701 --> 00:35:22,760
a chance to submit their bids too.

443
00:35:24,683 --> 00:35:27,560
What do you think the chances of success are?

444
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:28,760
One hundred percent, of course.

445
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:32,071
In the initial phase,

446
00:35:32,171 --> 00:35:34,840
we'll combine services from all three ministries:

447
00:35:34,860 --> 00:35:37,880
finance, healthcare, and transportation, all on one card.

448
00:35:38,168 --> 00:35:41,960
My party already oversees all three ministries, so there won't be any problems.

449
00:35:42,571 --> 00:35:44,080
- That's wonderful.
- That's great news.

450
00:35:44,507 --> 00:35:47,880
This project has always been your party's flagship policy.

451
00:35:48,022 --> 00:35:49,397
If you become Prime Minister in the next term,

452
00:35:49,558 --> 00:35:52,910
could all government services be integrated into a single card?

453
00:35:53,342 --> 00:35:55,680
- That's a good question.
- You've got my support!

454
00:35:56,328 --> 00:35:59,360
We're still serving under Prime Minister Narong.

455
00:35:59,502 --> 00:36:02,520
It wouldn't be appropriate to discuss the next term just yet.

456
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:04,840
Let's leave that for the future.

457
00:36:05,374 --> 00:36:08,640
When do you think the Smart Card will be launched?

458
00:36:08,835 --> 00:36:12,160
We've set a timeline of about three months.

459
00:36:12,411 --> 00:36:15,480
We should see some concrete progress by the middle of this year.

460
00:36:16,043 --> 00:36:17,360
I just can't picture it.

461
00:36:17,867 --> 00:36:20,680
This woman jumped over a table and tried to strangle you?

462
00:36:22,440 --> 00:36:24,120
I thought she'd send someone to attack you.

463
00:36:24,446 --> 00:36:25,600
Too bad we didn't get any evidence.

464
00:36:27,646 --> 00:36:30,200
The government's term is almost over, and elections are coming up.

465
00:36:30,600 --> 00:36:32,800
She's probably being careful to avoid any scandals.

466
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:37,700
We need to find a way to mess with her career.

467
00:36:40,283 --> 00:36:42,284
Why don't we bid on her Smart Card project?

468
00:36:42,638 --> 00:36:44,080
It's her biggest project, you know.

469
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:48,360
No way. Government contracts require deep pockets

470
00:36:48,883 --> 00:36:50,080
because payments take forever.

471
00:36:50,387 --> 00:36:53,520
A small company like ours doesn't stand a chance.

472
00:37:07,275 --> 00:37:08,500
I'm here to see the Minister.

473
00:37:08,944 --> 00:37:10,245
She's busy all day.

474
00:37:10,747 --> 00:37:12,158
You can leave a message with me.

475
00:37:13,214 --> 00:37:14,815
Then please tell her

476
00:37:15,107 --> 00:37:18,108
I've agreed to take the money and stay away from the Director.

477
00:37:23,707 --> 00:37:25,408
Don't believe her, ma'am. That homewrecking bitch.

478
00:37:25,846 --> 00:37:28,160
You'd be better off trusting a thief than her.

479
00:37:32,678 --> 00:37:34,079
But I don't want to miss this opportunity.

480
00:37:35,552 --> 00:37:37,350
She's finally accepted our offer.

481
00:37:40,374 --> 00:37:44,400
Then I guess I'll take a chance and be a fool to trust her.

482
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:53,376
Veekit.

483
00:37:56,984 --> 00:37:58,264
Hey, Veekit.

484
00:37:59,747 --> 00:38:00,748
Still mad at me?

485
00:38:03,688 --> 00:38:06,691
You look even more like an alpaca when you're angry.

486
00:38:14,478 --> 00:38:15,479
It's not funny.

487
00:38:16,100 --> 00:38:18,160
You stuffed Uncle Phop into that cabinet without telling me.

488
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,301
How do you think I'm supposed to feel?

489
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:23,501
Amused, maybe?

490
00:38:23,824 --> 00:38:26,160
I just wanted our show to be the talk of the town.

491
00:38:30,859 --> 00:38:32,960
You were deliberately trying to provoke Aunt Napha. I could tell.

492
00:38:34,235 --> 00:38:35,680
I've noticed it several times now, Ta.

493
00:38:37,243 --> 00:38:38,520
Why are you doing this? Just tell me.

494
00:38:41,995 --> 00:38:43,240
You're not my guardian.

495
00:38:44,160 --> 00:38:47,520
You don't get to watch my every move or control what I do.

496
00:38:48,246 --> 00:38:49,659
If you're that upset with me,

497
00:38:50,134 --> 00:38:51,720
- Then let's just stay out of each other's lives.
- No, no.

498
00:38:53,798 --> 00:38:55,640
I never said I didn't want anything to do with you.

499
00:38:56,966 --> 00:38:57,967
I just feel like

500
00:38:59,221 --> 00:39:01,046
I need to be more careful around you, that's all.

501
00:39:02,470 --> 00:39:04,760
If it's that much trouble, I won't bother you anymore.

502
00:39:09,471 --> 00:39:10,472
That's mine.

503
00:39:18,357 --> 00:39:20,320
Would you like to have lunch with me?

504
00:39:21,056 --> 00:39:23,720
- I've already eaten.
- Who are you here to see? Me?

505
00:39:23,757 --> 00:39:24,760
I'm here to see Mutta.

506
00:39:26,496 --> 00:39:28,480
Oh, Ta!

507
00:39:28,571 --> 00:39:30,360
Where have you been slacking off?

508
00:39:30,558 --> 00:39:32,280
Thaithat has been waiting for you.

509
00:39:32,675 --> 00:39:34,960
Yes. She wants to see you right away.

510
00:39:35,278 --> 00:39:36,440
Are you busy with anything?

511
00:39:37,864 --> 00:39:39,400
No, I'm free. I can go.

512
00:39:40,125 --> 00:39:41,126
Please take care of this for me.

513
00:39:50,230 --> 00:39:52,560
Hey, ladies, want to take a guess?

514
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:55,720
What do you think Mrs. Nopnapha

515
00:39:55,995 --> 00:39:57,296
is going to scold her for?

516
00:39:57,300 --> 00:39:59,920
Maybe she's not calling her in to scold her.

517
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:03,357
Maybe she's giving her a pay raise.

518
00:40:04,486 --> 00:40:06,180
More like a pay cut!

519
00:40:06,627 --> 00:40:07,628
Hey, Meow.

520
00:40:07,726 --> 00:40:10,080
How are we supposed to find out

521
00:40:10,527 --> 00:40:12,240
what Nopnapha's going to scold her for?

522
00:40:15,640 --> 00:40:16,800
What's so hard about that?

523
00:40:17,165 --> 00:40:21,040
Just turn into a fruit fly,

524
00:40:21,066 --> 00:40:22,600
buzz around them, and find out, you idiot.

525
00:40:23,280 --> 00:40:24,479
But I know something.

526
00:40:24,821 --> 00:40:25,822
Oops.

527
00:40:31,294 --> 00:40:35,480
Well, I overheard someone talking about it.

528
00:40:35,656 --> 00:40:36,657
- What did they say?
- What did they say?

529
00:40:38,968 --> 00:40:40,320
Apparently,

530
00:40:41,112 --> 00:40:44,280
Mrs. Nopnapha was furious about the New Year's party.

531
00:40:45,227 --> 00:40:49,275
Ta deliberately lured the Director into the cabinet

532
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:51,400
and made him come out

533
00:40:53,616 --> 00:40:55,840
with a sex doll to humiliate her.

534
00:40:58,952 --> 00:41:00,320
And that's not all.

535
00:41:01,374 --> 00:41:04,185
They also said the underwear the doll was wearing

536
00:41:04,935 --> 00:41:06,591
belonged to Ta.

537
00:41:09,670 --> 00:41:12,360
I really didn't want to spread any gossip.

538
00:41:12,811 --> 00:41:17,115
But since you're all so curious, I thought I'd share just a little.

539
00:41:19,798 --> 00:41:20,799
Everyone!

540
00:41:21,495 --> 00:41:23,300
Please don't tell anyone, okay?

541
00:41:23,496 --> 00:41:25,520
- Okay.
- Okay.

542
00:41:54,915 --> 00:41:58,120
You said my husband was worth more than ten million in bed.

543
00:41:59,902 --> 00:42:02,320
Has the sex gotten boring? Is that why you changed your mind?

544
00:42:04,158 --> 00:42:05,480
I owe you an apology.

545
00:42:05,635 --> 00:42:08,024
I only said that to get under your skin.

546
00:42:08,616 --> 00:42:09,800
I've come to my senses now.

547
00:42:10,069 --> 00:42:12,837
Money is more important than any man.

548
00:42:13,424 --> 00:42:14,725
Don't you agree, ma'am?

549
00:42:16,310 --> 00:42:17,600
Why didn't you realize that sooner?

550
00:42:18,475 --> 00:42:20,176
I didn't need the money back then.

551
00:42:27,950 --> 00:42:29,480
And how can I be sure

552
00:42:30,846 --> 00:42:32,080
that once you get the money,

553
00:42:33,043 --> 00:42:34,600
you'll really leave my husband alone?

554
00:42:37,192 --> 00:42:40,320
All I can give you is my word.

555
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:42,401
I'm a woman of my word.

556
00:43:34,395 --> 00:43:36,880
Someone go ask that homewrecking bitch what happened to her.

557
00:43:40,091 --> 00:43:42,520
Meow, with that foul mouth of yours, you're perfect for the job.

558
00:43:44,910 --> 00:43:47,960
Oh, no way! Look at her face. I'm scared she'll snap at me.

559
00:43:48,112 --> 00:43:50,600
Whisky, you're the closest to her. Go ask!

560
00:43:52,400 --> 00:43:55,560
The closer we are, the less I should ask.

561
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:59,120
Chuenchom, you're always asking stupid questions anyway.

562
00:43:59,339 --> 00:44:00,440
Why don't you go ask her?

563
00:44:01,691 --> 00:44:04,320
- Yeah!
- Exactly!

564
00:44:08,486 --> 00:44:11,240
You're all just as curious about Ta as I am.

565
00:44:11,400 --> 00:44:13,920
Why am I the only one who has to ask?

566
00:44:19,534 --> 00:44:21,360
Why are you all so nosy about other people's business?

567
00:44:22,104 --> 00:44:23,720
Will knowing the answer make your lives any better?

568
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:27,038
Well...

569
00:44:27,342 --> 00:44:29,243
We're Thai, after all.

570
00:44:29,270 --> 00:44:31,320
It's only natural to take an interest in other people's lives.

571
00:44:31,830 --> 00:44:34,531
We just noticed you looked stressed earlier.

572
00:44:34,731 --> 00:44:36,840
We thought maybe there was something we could help with.

573
00:44:39,718 --> 00:44:40,719
Actually,

574
00:44:41,750 --> 00:44:44,151
the Minister called me in to receive an Outstanding Civil Servant Award.

575
00:44:46,200 --> 00:44:48,520
For minding my own damn business.

576
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:54,320
- Ten million.
- Ten million.

577
00:44:58,648 --> 00:44:59,840
- Ten million.
- Ten million.

578
00:45:20,491 --> 00:45:21,700
Here's your chamomile tea, ma'am.

579
00:45:26,846 --> 00:45:27,987
I'd like a sleeping pill tonight.

580
00:45:30,387 --> 00:45:31,388
Of course, ma'am.

581
00:45:32,763 --> 00:45:33,764
Do you think

582
00:45:34,902 --> 00:45:37,000
someone like her will keep her word?

583
00:45:40,539 --> 00:45:42,720
I don't mean to stress you out even more, ma'am.

584
00:45:44,728 --> 00:45:46,300
But if I'm being realistic,

585
00:45:48,083 --> 00:45:49,200
it's hard to believe she will.

586
00:45:52,734 --> 00:45:53,960
Then make that two pills.

587
00:45:55,470 --> 00:45:56,471
Of course.

588
00:45:57,662 --> 00:45:58,800
But even if it's unlikely,

589
00:46:00,360 --> 00:46:01,880
there's still a chance, right?

590
00:46:05,224 --> 00:46:06,720
You'll have to put her to the test, ma'am.

591
00:46:08,334 --> 00:46:09,800
Whenever there's a long weekend,

592
00:46:10,254 --> 00:46:12,600
Mr. Jenphop usually takes Mutta on a trip.

593
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:17,601
There's a substitute holiday this weekend.

594
00:46:18,688 --> 00:46:20,089
Why don't you ask him

595
00:46:21,579 --> 00:46:22,760
if he's planning to go anywhere?

596
00:46:36,371 --> 00:46:37,680
Mommy!

597
00:46:38,286 --> 00:46:41,087
For my birthday, I want this Bambinana Red Hat.

598
00:46:44,080 --> 00:46:45,081
Okay.

599
00:46:45,481 --> 00:46:47,082
Go to bed, sweetie. I have a headache.

600
00:46:47,926 --> 00:46:51,520
You have to buy it on the 25th. It's only on sale that day.

601
00:46:51,883 --> 00:46:53,760
I'll have Oshi take care of it.

602
00:46:55,523 --> 00:46:56,640
Don't forget!

603
00:47:01,683 --> 00:47:02,840
The 25th, okay?

604
00:47:02,884 --> 00:47:03,920
Okay.

605
00:47:21,776 --> 00:47:22,777
Yes, Director?

606
00:47:22,928 --> 00:47:25,360
Ta, let's go to Hong Kong over the long weekend.

607
00:47:27,339 --> 00:47:29,200
I haven't taken you shopping in ages.

608
00:47:29,600 --> 00:47:32,400
Oh, and I'll take you to your favorite dim sum restaurant too.

609
00:47:33,595 --> 00:47:34,840
And after we're done eating, we can...

610
00:47:35,883 --> 00:47:37,040
have some fun.

611
00:47:37,500 --> 00:47:39,320
Fun... the kind of fun...

612
00:47:40,278 --> 00:47:42,200
without anyone getting in our way this time.

613
00:47:44,032 --> 00:47:45,033
I'd rather not.

614
00:47:45,336 --> 00:47:48,080
Director, I think we should take a break.

615
00:47:48,360 --> 00:47:49,520
And please don't contact me again.

616
00:47:49,822 --> 00:47:51,623
I'm blocking you on everything.

617
00:47:51,950 --> 00:47:52,951
- Bye.
- What?

618
00:47:54,151 --> 00:47:56,200
Blocking me? Ta...

619
00:47:56,688 --> 00:47:58,889
Ta? Hello? Hello?

620
00:48:00,363 --> 00:48:01,364
What the hell? Why'd she block me?

621
00:48:04,912 --> 00:48:06,800
Honey, are you asleep?

622
00:48:07,592 --> 00:48:08,593
Wait, wait.

623
00:48:21,883 --> 00:48:22,884
What is it?

624
00:48:25,771 --> 00:48:27,640
I'm having a barbecue this Saturday.

625
00:48:28,416 --> 00:48:29,417
Are you free?

626
00:48:32,480 --> 00:48:35,046
Yeah, I'm free.

627
00:48:36,139 --> 00:48:37,140
I'm not going anywhere.

628
00:48:39,712 --> 00:48:40,713
That sounds nice.

629
00:48:41,574 --> 00:48:42,960
We haven't had a barbecue in ages.

630
00:48:45,550 --> 00:48:47,440
I wonder if the grill still works.

631
00:48:48,430 --> 00:48:49,431
I'll go check.

632
00:49:03,734 --> 00:49:05,960
Ta, what did I do wrong?

633
00:49:06,735 --> 00:49:07,840
Can you please tell me?

634
00:49:11,283 --> 00:49:13,080
Your silence is really worrying me.

635
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,760
Dad, can you come take a look now?

636
00:49:17,264 --> 00:49:18,265
Go ask your mom.

637
00:49:18,700 --> 00:49:19,701
Come on!

638
00:49:21,782 --> 00:49:24,523
Whenever we ask you anything, you always tell us to ask Mom.

639
00:49:24,783 --> 00:49:25,784
What's your problem?

640
00:49:33,147 --> 00:49:35,270
Yeah, it's ready. Take it off the grill.

641
00:49:35,707 --> 00:49:37,708
Nice and juicy. Just right.

642
00:49:40,312 --> 00:49:41,960
What have you kids been cooking?

643
00:49:43,688 --> 00:49:44,920
Oh my goodness!

644
00:49:45,123 --> 00:49:48,160
It's still so red! You can't eat that! You'll get sick!

645
00:49:48,744 --> 00:49:50,440
But Dad said it was ready.

646
00:49:50,600 --> 00:49:51,601
He said it was nice and juicy.

647
00:49:52,147 --> 00:49:54,250
Oh, for goodness' sake!

648
00:49:56,280 --> 00:49:58,521
Honey, come here.

649
00:50:05,549 --> 00:50:07,848
My party oversees the Ministry of Health.

650
00:50:08,264 --> 00:50:10,920
Wouldn't it be embarrassing

651
00:50:11,019 --> 00:50:12,130
if our whole family ended up with tapeworms?

652
00:50:12,140 --> 00:50:13,720
Are you crazy? How can you eat that?

653
00:50:15,641 --> 00:50:17,000
Oh my gosh!

654
00:50:17,323 --> 00:50:19,760
Kids, you can't eat meat that looks like this.

655
00:50:20,635 --> 00:50:24,560
- So much for Dad's juicy meat. We'll get diarrhea.
- Spaghetti's ready!

656
00:50:25,664 --> 00:50:27,963
- It's piping hot! Come and get it.
- Veekit.

657
00:50:28,697 --> 00:50:30,198
Veekit.

658
00:50:30,531 --> 00:50:32,200
Could you serve some for me too?

659
00:50:32,286 --> 00:50:34,560
Just a little, though. I don't want to gain weight.

660
00:50:34,880 --> 00:50:35,981
Sure.

661
00:50:36,120 --> 00:50:37,886
Can you make me some punch?

662
00:50:37,920 --> 00:50:39,934
Not too sweet, please. I'm watching my weight too.

663
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:41,001
Okay.

664
00:50:56,456 --> 00:50:57,960
Oh, Tetris!

665
00:50:58,275 --> 00:51:00,470
Dance more like a man. You're a real man, after all.

666
00:51:00,478 --> 00:51:01,479
Here, like this.

667
00:51:03,704 --> 00:51:05,160
- One, two, three!
- Manly, right?

668
00:51:06,275 --> 00:51:08,000
- Manly!
- Manly! Okay!

669
00:51:14,500 --> 00:51:15,501
Phop.

670
00:51:17,611 --> 00:51:20,200
Why don't we have a barbecue like this every long weekend?

671
00:51:20,528 --> 00:51:23,880
I'll try to free up more time for the family.

672
00:51:27,200 --> 00:51:28,201
Whatever you want.

673
00:51:28,700 --> 00:51:30,001
I'm fine with whatever you decide.

674
00:51:40,278 --> 00:51:41,279
Actually,

675
00:51:41,958 --> 00:51:45,560
having fun can be as simple as this, Phop.

676
00:51:54,187 --> 00:51:55,188
Don't you think?

677
00:51:56,294 --> 00:51:57,680
Try to relax your face.

678
00:52:00,048 --> 00:52:02,320
That's better. Much better.

679
00:52:04,672 --> 00:52:05,673
Mom!

680
00:52:06,422 --> 00:52:07,760
Come do a TikTok dance with us!

681
00:52:08,459 --> 00:52:10,880
Go on, Phop. Have some fun dancing with the kids.

682
00:52:12,060 --> 00:52:14,200
Oh, no. You go ahead.

683
00:52:14,920 --> 00:52:16,960
If I tried, it'd look more like physical therapy than dancing.

684
00:52:17,886 --> 00:52:18,887
Go on.

685
00:52:20,904 --> 00:52:21,905
Come on!

686
00:52:26,024 --> 00:52:27,400
She can take my place.

687
00:52:27,880 --> 00:52:29,200
- I'm going to take a break.
- Hey, where are you going?

688
00:52:29,400 --> 00:52:31,720
- You're sneaking off!
- Nice escape!

689
00:52:32,622 --> 00:52:33,623
Come on.

690
00:52:35,600 --> 00:52:37,201
- Come dance with us.
- Okay.

691
00:52:37,926 --> 00:52:38,927
Dance like a man.

692
00:52:42,880 --> 00:52:44,241
Aren't you going to dance with the kids?

693
00:52:46,784 --> 00:52:48,250
I'm not in the mood to dance anymore.

694
00:52:51,776 --> 00:52:52,777
Hey, Veekit.

695
00:52:54,520 --> 00:52:55,760
Have you talked to Ta lately?

696
00:52:56,206 --> 00:52:57,207
No, I haven't.

697
00:52:58,307 --> 00:52:59,640
I think she's upset with me.

698
00:53:01,155 --> 00:53:02,240
Why would she be upset with you?

699
00:53:03,102 --> 00:53:04,326
Well, I got mad at her

700
00:53:04,720 --> 00:53:07,360
for stripping you and stuffing you into that cabinet.

701
00:53:08,675 --> 00:53:10,120
So now she's upset with me for getting mad at her.

702
00:53:12,336 --> 00:53:13,960
Why do you ask, Uncle Phop?

703
00:53:16,470 --> 00:53:19,840
She suddenly blocked me on everything.

704
00:53:20,656 --> 00:53:23,157
She didn't even tell me why. I don't know what's wrong.

705
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:27,187
I'm afraid she'll disappear again like last time.

706
00:53:35,043 --> 00:53:36,360
Want me to ask her for you?

707
00:53:46,438 --> 00:53:47,439
Hello, Ta.

708
00:53:49,734 --> 00:53:53,480
Uncle Phop just wants to know what's wrong.

709
00:53:54,078 --> 00:53:56,240
Why aren't you talking to him anymore?

710
00:53:58,184 --> 00:53:59,440
Huh? Really?

711
00:54:00,635 --> 00:54:01,636
Oh, I see.

712
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:03,081
Okay, okay.

713
00:54:04,526 --> 00:54:06,640
Uncle Phop, Ta said

714
00:54:06,798 --> 00:54:09,171
she wants to cut ties with you for good.

715
00:54:09,448 --> 00:54:11,280
What? No way!

716
00:54:11,683 --> 00:54:12,684
Give me that.

717
00:54:13,107 --> 00:54:15,320
Ta, sweetheart. Ta.

718
00:54:15,360 --> 00:54:18,561
How could you do this to me? What's going on, Ta?

719
00:54:19,984 --> 00:54:20,985
Ta? Hello?

720
00:54:23,846 --> 00:54:24,847
Hey, Veekit!

721
00:54:27,296 --> 00:54:30,000
Why does it say the number I'm calling is unavailable?

722
00:54:30,939 --> 00:54:32,880
I was just messing with you. She didn't answer.

723
00:54:37,846 --> 00:54:38,920
You little punk.

724
00:54:42,246 --> 00:54:43,400
I'm stressed enough as it is.

725
00:54:51,806 --> 00:54:53,407
Since we announced the project,

726
00:54:53,410 --> 00:54:55,960
we've received applications from 86 developers.

727
00:54:56,312 --> 00:54:57,747
Both large and small companies.

728
00:54:57,813 --> 00:54:59,720
Their levels of experience vary.

729
00:55:06,374 --> 00:55:09,560
What if we award the contract to a small company

730
00:55:09,739 --> 00:55:12,240
with limited capital, run by young startup entrepreneurs?

731
00:55:12,640 --> 00:55:13,641
What do you think?

732
00:55:13,741 --> 00:55:14,742
That would be great.

733
00:55:14,837 --> 00:55:16,638
It would directly boost your public image,

734
00:55:17,020 --> 00:55:19,521
showing you're not favoring big corporations or colluding with powerful figures.

735
00:55:19,958 --> 00:55:22,080
You'll definitely win support from Gen Z voters.

736
00:55:23,238 --> 00:55:25,240
Okay, then...

737
00:55:25,603 --> 00:55:29,040
Find me some promising young companies with strong profiles.

738
00:55:29,198 --> 00:55:30,640
And when the e-bidding takes place,

739
00:55:30,760 --> 00:55:32,661
make sure the system is rigged without anyone noticing.

740
00:55:35,251 --> 00:55:36,252
Director.

741
00:55:37,078 --> 00:55:39,360
Ta! What kind of prank are you pulling on me this time?

742
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:41,181
One minute you're gone, the next you're back.

743
00:55:41,424 --> 00:55:42,425
I don't know what to think anymore.

744
00:55:43,296 --> 00:55:46,520
Keeping you guessing makes our love more exciting.

745
00:55:49,000 --> 00:55:50,621
There's a package for you, ma'am.

746
00:55:52,344 --> 00:55:53,720
Thanks, handsome.

747
00:56:02,926 --> 00:56:06,000
Ma'am, that bitch Mutta sent you a package.

748
00:56:06,435 --> 00:56:08,360
Be careful. It could be dangerous.

749
00:56:11,208 --> 00:56:12,209
Sorry, ma'am.

750
00:56:35,456 --> 00:56:36,457
What is it, Touch?

751
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:41,467
Money. There must be millions in here.

752
00:56:51,822 --> 00:56:52,823
Oh my gosh!

753
00:56:53,730 --> 00:56:56,120
Ma'am, our informant just sent us these photos.

754
00:56:56,339 --> 00:56:57,940
This just happened.

755
00:57:07,158 --> 00:57:08,360
That bitch Mutta!

756
00:57:20,832 --> 00:57:24,250
Since you came back, we haven't had sex even once.

757
00:57:25,120 --> 00:57:26,960
I'm not letting you put me off any longer.

758
00:57:27,328 --> 00:57:29,560
Wait, Director. Let's have a few drinks first.

759
00:57:32,240 --> 00:57:34,880
If you've got something good, you should share it.

760
00:57:34,998 --> 00:57:36,960
When I'm done with him, you can have him back.

761
00:57:37,451 --> 00:57:39,360
It's not like he's going to wear out.

762
00:57:40,131 --> 00:57:41,132
You bitch!

763
00:57:42,190 --> 00:57:43,191
Ms. Nin.

764
00:57:44,232 --> 00:57:45,233
I have to go now.

765
00:57:45,400 --> 00:57:46,691
Ta! Ta, wait!

766
00:57:46,840 --> 00:57:49,840
Do either of you know someone named Nin?

767
00:57:50,083 --> 00:57:51,320
Hong, do you know which Nin he's talking about?

768
00:57:51,600 --> 00:57:52,601
Nin...

769
00:57:54,536 --> 00:57:56,216
I'm going to use her daughter against her.

770
00:57:56,300 --> 00:57:57,560
What are you going to do to that girl?

771
00:57:58,640 --> 00:58:00,040
Oh! The pretty sister is here.

772
00:58:07,341 --> 00:58:08,342
Shit!
